    myth: '"You need a very high score to get any medical seat."',
    watchLabel: 'Why it misleads: marks are rarely the wall for private seats. Money is.',
    truth: 'Only 90,780 candidates scored 500 or more in 2026, which is fewer than the roughly 1,36,939 MBBS seats. Private and deemed seats have closed near 300 marks. The real barrier is fee, not marks, and it is steep: management-quota tuition of Rs 55 lakh to Rs 1.35 crore.',
  },
  {
