  <h2 id="answer">The direct answer: sort by the rule, then by your score band</h2>

  <p>
    Most pages on career options after 12th without NEET give you fifteen courses and one line each. That is not
    where students get stuck. They get stuck because the same page calls nursing, physiotherapy and optometry
    "NEET-free" when the rules differ by state, by year and by regulator.
  </p>

  <p>
    A better order is the rule first, your NEET score band second, then the paths ranked by how far they can grow,
    with pay and fee numbers you can check.
  </p>

