  <h3>A first test that fits your pace</h3>

  <p>
    Pick one path and do a small real thing. Spend a day with a working nurse, a physiotherapist, a lab head or
    a food-plant supervisor. Read one course syllabus fully. Sit one full timed mock of the exam you would need.
    Do it for as long as it takes to get honest feedback. Some students need a few weeks, others a couple of
    months, and both are normal.
  </p>

  <div class="gates-block">
    <p class="gates-block__title">The 3 Gates: pass these before you commit money or a drop year.</p>
    <div class="gates-row">
